  "cves": [
    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-107226",
      "publishedDate": "2026-10-12T18:34:18.996Z",
      "lastModifiedDate": "2026-10-12T18:34:18.996Z",
      "description": "The AsyncHttpClient (AHC) library allows Java applications to easily execute HTTP requests and asynchronously process HTTP responses. From 2.1.0 until 3.0.14, the default ThreadSafeCookieStore does not retain whether a Set-Cookie response used a secure transport. It accepts Secure cookies received over plaintext and permits insecure cookies to overlay or delete existing Secure cookies with matching scope. An attacker controlling a plaintext same-site response can consequently plant, replace, or remove cookie state later sent to an HTTPS origin, enabling session fixation, CSRF-token replacement, or loss of security-relevant state. This issue is fixed in version 3.0.14.",
      "severity": 6.8,
      "fix_suggestion": "📦 受影响组件：AsyncHttpClient async-http-client\n🔓 漏洞类型：CWE-384, CWE-693 (CWE-384, CWE-693)\n🛠️ 修复建议：\n1. 确认受影响的版本范围（见上方 Affected Products）\n2. 升级到厂商官方发布的最稳定安全版本\n3. 检查官方安全公告获取补丁链接\n4. 如无法立即升级，实施临时缓解措施：\n   - 网络层：WAF 规则 / IPS 签名 / 零信任策略\n   - 主机层：最小化暴露面 / 禁用危险功能 / 输入过滤\n5. 修复后使用 NVD / 厂商 PoC 验证修复有效性",
      "references": [
        {
          "url": "https://github.com/AsyncHttpClient/async-http-client/security/advisories/GHSA-p2jm-6hj6-9rjg",
